{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" xmlns:datamodel=\"https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/datamodel\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"json\" datamodel:src=\"urn:example:datamodels:json\" initial=\"a\">\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <transition event=\"go\" target=\"done\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"done\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/pkg005-unbound-data-model-package.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/pkg005-unbound-data-model-package.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":201,"endLine":1,"startColumn":174,"startLine":1}}}],"message":{"markdown":"no data-model package binds `urn:example:datamodels:json`\n\n**Note:** the data model's package did not resolve and no `--data-model-package` binds this URI, so none of this machine's expressions can be evaluated\n\n**Help:** bind the package with `--data-model-package MANIFEST.json`, or name a repository data model whose release resolves\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.1 Data Model","text":"no data-model package binds `urn:example:datamodels:json`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":200,"start":173},"category":"package"},"ruleId":"PKG005"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §5.1 lets a document choose its data model with the `datamodel` token; this toolchain builds in `ecmascript`, `null`, and `xpath`, and any other data model is a package named on the same `<scxml>` by `datamodel:src` (`https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/datamodel`), resolved like other packages. A token that names neither (often a typo of a built-in one), a `datamodel:src` that is no tagless absolute URI, or one no given data-model package binds (its repository release did not resolve) fails closed, because none of the machine's expressions could be evaluated. The value is `xsd:NMTOKEN`, whose white space collapses (XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), so `datamodel=\" xpath \"` is `xpath`"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: use a built-in data model, or name the data model's package with `datamodel:src` and make sure it resolves (or bind it with `--data-model-package MANIFEST.json`).\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.1 Data Model\n\nRun `scx --explain PKG005` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#data-module","id":"PKG005","name":"PKG005","properties":{"category":"package"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a machine's data model is neither built in nor available from a package"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}